/CLAUDE.md              @ianshank

# Governance surfaces. The charter is supreme, the evidence artifacts are what
# every numeric claim resolves to, and the baselines are what CI gates against --
# a change to any of them is a change to what this project claims, so it is
# routed for review even when the diff looks like a data file.
#
# Routing, not enforcement: every path here resolves to the same single owner,
# and CODEOWNERS cannot separate an author from an approver when there is one of
# them. The value is that a governance change is never invisible in the file
# list. Genuine author/approver separation needs distinct GitHub identities plus
# admin-enforced branch protection, none of which is repository-side config.
/openspec/              @ianshank
/evidence/              @ianshank
/results/               @ianshank
/config/baselines/      @ianshank
/config/focus.yaml      @ianshank
/docs/FOCUS.md          @ianshank
/docs/adr/              @ianshank

# CI / tooling
/.github/               @ianshank
/pyproject.toml         @ianshank
